- terminal_picker_cc
    - Status: 🟡 MVP
    - Mode: 🤖 Claude Code
    - Updated: 2026-10-08

- Overview
    - A Claude-Code-style interactive picker for shell scripts.
    - Shows a list of options with arrow-key navigation. With --custom, an inline textbox row is added: when focused, typing goes straight into it, no extra Enter to enter "edit mode".
    - The textbox is the last row by default, or the first row with --custom-first.
    - Options can carry a separate display string (VALUE<TAB>DISPLAY) with light inline color/attribute markup, so lists can render as colored tables (e.g. icons, aligned columns, a status tag) while still returning a clean value.
    - Single-file Python script using stdlib curses, no third-party deps.
    - Spaces (and any printable ASCII) are valid input in the textbox.

- Why
    - fzf is a fuzzy filter, not a list picker, and gum is an extra install.
    - Claude Code's AskUserQuestion UI (arrow nav with an inline "Other" textbox) does not exist as a shell tool.
    - This package reproduces that UX in a small reusable CLI, now with enough styling to stand in for fzf-as-list-picker.

- Install
    - Option 1: symlink onto your PATH
        - ln -s /home/$USER/public/terminal_picker_cc/picker /home/$USER/.local/bin/picker
    - Option 2: add this directory to PATH in your shell rc
        - export PATH="$PATH:/home/$USER/public/terminal_picker_cc"
    - Option 3: call it by absolute path from your scripts
        - /home/$USER/public/terminal_picker_cc/picker --custom foo bar

- Usage
    - picker [--header TEXT] [--custom] [--custom-first] [--custom-label TEXT] [--default N] [--marker STR] [ITEM ...]
    - Items can be passed as args or piped on stdin (one per line).
    - Selection is printed to stdout. Cancel (Esc / Ctrl+C) exits with code 130.
    - Flags
        - --header TEXT: bold header above the list, supports newlines
        - --custom: add an inline textbox row that accepts typed input the moment it is focused
        - --custom-first: place the textbox row at the top instead of the bottom
        - --custom-label TEXT: placeholder shown in the textbox when empty and unfocused (supports markup)
        - --default N: which option starts highlighted (0-based, default 0)
        - --marker STR: prefix shown next to the highlighted line (default "> ")

- Item format
    - ITEM: value and display are the same (backward compatible)
    - VALUE<TAB>DISPLAY: VALUE is returned on select; DISPLAY is rendered, with markup
    - Example: "dev\t{cyan}●{/}  dev                  2 windows  {yellow}(attached){/}"

- Colors and text attributes
    - DISPLAY supports {token} markup. {/} resets to normal.
    - Colors: {black} {red} {green} {yellow} {blue} {magenta} {cyan} {white}
    - Attributes: {bold} {dim} {underline} {reverse}
    - Unknown tokens are shown literally. Color tokens are stripped when the terminal cannot do color.
    - The selected row is shown bold; colors are preserved.

- Keybindings
    - up / down: move highlight (wraps)
    - k / j: same as up / down, but only when not focused on the textbox slot (so j and k can be typed into the textbox)
    - enter: confirm the highlighted option, or, when on the textbox with non-empty content, return what was typed; enter on an empty textbox does nothing
    - on textbox: any printable ASCII (including space) is appended; backspace deletes; the buffer is preserved if you arrow away and come back
    - esc / ctrl+c: cancel the picker (exit 130)

- Examples
    - Plain list from args
        - choice=$(picker --header "Pick one" apple banana cherry)
    - List from stdin
        - choice=$(ls /etc | picker --header "Files in /etc")
    - With a custom-input fallback
        - folder=$(picker --header "Pick or type a folder" --custom drafts inbox archive)
    - Type-to-create first, colored table
        - picker --custom --custom-first --custom-label "{green}+{/}  {dim}new name...{/}" \
              "dev\t{cyan}●{/}  dev   2 windows  {yellow}(attached){/}" "notes"
    - Detect custom vs listed value
        - selection=$(picker --custom apple banana)
        - case "$selection" in apple|banana) echo "picked from list" ;; "") echo "cancelled" ;; *) echo "typed: $selection" ;; esac

- Implementation Notes
    - Uses curses from the Python stdlib, so works on any system with python3.
    - Reads keys and renders to /dev/tty so that the caller can capture stdout: selection=$(picker ...) works as expected.
    - Stdin can carry the option list because it is consumed before /dev/tty is dup'd onto fd 0.
    - init_colors builds a color pair per named color using use_default_colors when available; parse_segments turns markup into (chunk, attr) runs that render blits left to right with width clipping.

- Files
    - picker: the executable script
    - readme.log: this file
    - STATUS.log: project status
    - CLAUDE.md: project conventions

- Consumers
    - tmux_setting: bin/tm-picker and bin/tm-login use it for the tmux session picker (colored table with a type-to-create row first). tm-picker falls back to a plain-text chooser if the picker is absent.

- Known Limitations
    - No multi-select.
    - No filter-as-you-type (intentional, this is a picker, not a fuzzy finder).
    - Only ASCII printable characters (including space) are accepted in the textbox; no unicode input.
    - No scrolling for very long lists.
